        "original_id": "d07bc261-ded4-5792-9d5b-5ebbfa3d9d43",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Memphis International Airport, Southwest Georgia Regional Airport, Albany, Memphis, Shelby County, Dougherty County, Tennessee, Georgia, United States, Boston, Massachusetts, New York\n- Systems: IATA, ICAO, FAA LID\n- Organizations: FedEx Express\n- Events: FedEx Express Flight 1406\n\nFacts:\n- Memphis International Airport has the codes IATA MEM, ICAO KMEM, and FAA LID MEM.\n- Memphis International Airport is a civil-military airport located seven miles southeast of downtown Memphis in Shelby County, Tennessee, United States.\n- Southwest Georgia Regional Airport has the codes IATA ABY, ICAO KABY, and FAA LID ABY.\n- Southwest Georgia Regional Airport is a city-owned public-use airport located three nautical miles southwest of the central business district of Albany in Dougherty County, Georgia, United States.\n- FedEx Express Flight 1406 was a cargo flight from Memphis International Airport in Memphis, Tennessee, to Logan International Airport in Boston, Massachusetts.\n- FedEx Express Flight 1406 suffered an in-flight cargo fire over New York.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
